<title>GREECE: Greek M3 rises provisionally 8.7 pct y/y in Oct.</title>
<headline>Greek M3 rises provisionally 8.7 pct y/y in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek M3 money supply grew a provisional 8.7 percent year-on-year in October versus 9.8 percent in September. This was within the central bank's 6.0-9.0 percent target range for end-96, the Bank of Greece said in a statement.</p>
<p>The M4 monetary aggregate grew provisionally 10.6 percent year-on-year in October after a provisional 7.7 percent rise in September, it said.</p>
<p>    M3 money supply		   Oct 96*   Sept 96*   Oct 95</p>
<p>    Stock (in bln drachmas)	 17,069    17,224	15,707</p>
<p>    Yr-on-yr (pct)			8.7	 9.8	   9.9</p>
<p>*  indicates provisional figures</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
